  "$note": "Proposed chain whitelist (DATA_SPEC.md §5.2). Rows exist for every kanji appearing in three or more entries plus every chain CLAUDE.md §5 names. Only the five chains CLAUDE.md §5 describes carry a rule; every other row is rule_reliability \"none\" until Dan rules on it in his study project, and nothing in the UI may present a \"none\" chain as a lesson.",
  "chains": [
    {
      "character": "手",
      "display_order": 1,
      "rule": "手 is て (kun) throughout; classification is determined entirely by the second character: on → 湯桶 (手本, 手帳, 手数), kun → 訓訓 (手紙, 手間).",
      "rule_reliability": "clean",
      "teaching_note": "Best introduction: the rule is statable in one sentence and shows the same character with the same reading classified by its partner alone. Order: the 訓訓 entries, then the 湯桶 entries. 手段 (しゅだん, 手 = シュ on) is in the dataset and contradicts \"throughout\"; it is placed last and the validator flags it for Dan to rule on.",
