    {
      "character": "場",
      "display_order": 2,
      "rule": "A character's reading type is not a fixed property: 場 is ジョウ (on) in 入場, 会場, 工場 and ば (kun) in 職場, 本場, 役場, 立場, 場面, 場所; the partner decides, and the classification shifts with it.",
      "rule_reliability": "usually",
      "teaching_note": "The richest chain, spanning four classifications, and the payoff chain. Build toward 場所 last: it is the signature trap — ば is kun, ジョウ is on; learners assume a short, high-frequency reading must be on and misclassify 場所 as 音音. The reliability value is a proposal (CLAUDE.md §5 gives none for 場); Dan to rule.",
